  receipts: [
    "**INVALID STATE: the required floor's changed-witness attribution charges a pure-deletion diff hunk to the UNCHANGED declaration that follows it, so deleting witnesses force-runs a neighbour whose text did not change.** The floor maps the PR's changed line ranges to declarations (`v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner` `floor_diff_edits_from_line_ranges_reading`). A deletion leaves no line in the head file; its range lands at the deletion point, which is the first line of the next declaration, so that declaration is attributed as edited.",

    "HARM: an unchanged, cost-withheld witness is run under `ChangedCostDebtVerdictOnly` with the 8s wall armed, and if its real cost exceeds the wall the floor reports INTERRUPTED-BEFORE-VERDICT and refuses the change. Nothing about the neighbour changed, so the red says nothing about the change, which is the FLOOR-CHANGED-COST-0 failure the changed-witness policy exists to prevent, reached through attribution rather than through the policy. Because any deletion between two declarations is adjacent to one of them, placement cannot avoid it: the only escapes today are an operator override or editing the neighbour into something cheaper, which widens the change beyond its subject.",

    "**SPECIMEN, measured 2026-10-03 on gunbc#13103 (advisories step 2) at head 8015248470.** Deleting `v2.test.claim.enforcement.grammar_coverage_witness`'s three v1-file `*_by_execution` claims (replaced by supplied-chain claims) left one deletion hunk directly above `grammar_coverage_v1_tree_receipt_by_execution`. The floor planned that claim as a changed witness (changed_witnesses=16, changed_witness_blocking=2) and interrupted it at the wall (wall 8009ms / 8000ms, cpu 6173ms), although its text and assertions were untouched. It went into the same one-time operator override as the long door-ledger claim, which hit the same wall for a different reason (`restoration_promise_names_a_route_that_does_not_exist`, third specimen).",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: not `restoration_promise_names_a_route_that_does_not_exist`, which is about the remedy text promising a lane that is absent. Here the remedy is irrelevant, because the witness should not have been selected at all. And not a cost defect of the neighbour: it was withheld honestly, and the floor's own roster says so.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: a changed-witness interruption whose identity has no line in the PR's diff of its own declaration, only an adjacent deletion, is this class.",

