    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a CAPABILITY: changed-witness attribution that classifies a pure-deletion hunk by the declarations it REMOVED (base side) rather than by the head-side line it lands on, so a deletion selects only the deleted identities (which no longer exist to run) and never an unchanged neighbour.",

    "**REPAIRED IN THE CHANGE THAT FOUND IT (gunbc#13103), after a reshape attempt failed.** Leaving a blank separator where the claims were deleted only moved the charge: the next run charged the PRECEDING claim (`grammar_coverage_dag_tree_receipt_by_execution`, wall 8010ms / 8000ms at head 18e2c4aa4b), because a declaration's attributed span ran to the next declaration's start and so owned the blank line. The repair is in the attribution: `v1_compiler.cli_run` `parse_unified_diff_line_ranges` marks a zero-width `-U0` range as `deletion_gap`. `v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner` `floor_diff_edits_from_line_ranges_reading` then charges a gap to a declaration only when the gap lies inside it, between its start and its last non-blank line; a gap at or before the first declaration stays a file-grain edit, and a gap between declarations charges nothing. The bound errs toward charging: a deleted leading comment of the next declaration charges the previous one. DISCRIMINATING CONTROLS: `a_deletion_between_declarations_charges_neither_neighbour` (red with gap handling disabled: it charged `c`) and `a_deletion_inside_a_declaration_still_charges_it` (an interior deletion still selects its declaration). RUNG NOW: 1 (mitigatable), NOT 2. The production behaviour is fixed, and the floor's own run on gunbc#13103 (a deletion-only change) executed it once. But the two controls are seed unit tests that no CI path runs (`gunbc.rung_drop` `rust_unit_tests_off_the_merge_path`), so nothing re-executes them on every change, and DESIGN section 4b(1) counts only enrolled, executing evidence. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a CAPABILITY: seed unit tests executing as a blocking lane on the merge path (the restoration that rung drop names). That enrols these controls, and the class reaches rung 2."
